---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../../utils/paths';

const pageTitle = "Text Replacements & Regular Expressions";
const pageDesc = "Ordered find and replace pairs, literal or regular expression, applied in one deterministic pass with Telegram entity offsets preserved.";
---

<DocsLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDesc}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Features', href: url('/features/') },
    { name: 'Replacements & Regex', href: url('/features/replacements-and-regex/') },
  ]}
  prev={{ title: 'Headers & Footers', href: url('/features/headers-footers-shortcodes/') }}
  next={{ title: 'Scheduling & Delays', href: url('/features/scheduling-and-delays/') }}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
    <p>
      The <strong>Replacement Engine</strong> enables fine-grained textual substitutions on incoming Telegram posts. This allows modifying brand names, re-tagging topics, or translating recurring phrases before broadcasting to your destination chats.
    </p>

    <h2 id="dictionary-replacements">Dictionary-Based Replacements</h2>
    <p>
      Define exact key-value pairs to replace across the message text and media captions:
    </p>
    <pre class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl text-xs font-mono text-emerald-400"><code># Example Dictionary Pairings
"Binance" -> "Crypto Exchange"
"Discount Code: ABC" -> "Discount Code: PROMO2026"
"Follow @OldChannel" -> "Follow @OurChannel"</code></pre>

    <h2 id="regex-substitutions">Regex Transformations</h2>
    <p>
      For dynamic patterns, AutoTelegramForward supports standard Python regex expressions:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Pattern Matching:</strong> <code>(?i)price:\s*\$([0-9.]+)</code></li>
      <li><strong>Group Substitution:</strong> <code>Valuation: $$1 USD</code></li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="redos-safety">Catastrophic Backtracking (ReDoS) Defense</h2>
    <p>
      User-supplied regular expressions can inadvertently cause CPU exhaustion (ReDoS). AutoTelegramForward validates every pattern against strict compilation limits and enforces an execution timeout on every regex substitution. If a pattern times out, it logs an error and gracefully preserves the original text without dropping the message.
    </p>

    <h2 id="entity-preservation">Telegram Entity Preservation</h2>
    <p>
      When performing textual modifications, naive string replacement breaks Telegram formatting entities (such as <code>MessageEntityBold</code>, <code>MessageEntityItalic</code>, or <code>MessageEntityCode</code>) because byte offsets shift. AutoTelegramForward re-calculates entity offsets or reconstructs formatted text in MarkdownV2/HTML mode to ensure typography remains crisp and uncorrupted.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
